Description: @DISTRIBUTION@ GNOME desktop metapackage
 Pulls in the GNOME desktop set @DISTRIBUTION@ curates: shell, file
 manager, terminal, system settings, browser (firefox-esr), common
 GNOME apps + utilities, PIM stack (calendar/contacts/clocks),
 software center, admin GUI tools, audio (pipewire), font fallback
 (Noto + DejaVu).
 .
 Also ships /etc/NetworkManager/conf.d/10-asgard-managed.conf so the
 GNOME Shell network indicator appears correctly on debootstrap-based
 installs where the installer left a non-loopback stanza in
 /etc/network/interfaces (NetworkManager would otherwise defer to
 ifupdown on that device, leave zero managed devices, and hide the
 indicator).  Postinst restarts NetworkManager so the drop-in takes
 effect without requiring a reboot.
 .
 Mirrors the [gnome-desktop] group in config/pkg.list so the same
 package set ships at install time (via the tasksel "GNOME Desktop"
 task) and post-install (via apt install asgard-gnome-desktop).
 .
 This is a Pattern B metapackage per docs/branding-methodology.md:
 operator-facing convenience that does NOT replace tasksel's Key
 list.  apt remove --autoremove asgard-gnome-desktop cleans up the
 whole group AND the NetworkManager conf.d drop-in.
